The following changes fix an issue where setting the `UaSettings.contact_uri` had no effect anymore.

In an older version of this library contact_uri was a String
```
'contact_uri': (Settings src, Settings? dst) {
      dynamic contact_uri = src.contact_uri;
      if (contact_uri == null) return;
      if (contact_uri is String) {
        dynamic uri = Grammar.parse(contact_uri, 'SIP_URI');
        if (uri != -1) {
          dst!.contact_uri = uri;
        }
      }
```

In the latest version `src.contact_uri` is an `URI?`. Therefore checking for a `String` doesn't make sense anymore and leads to `dst.contact_uri` being always null.

## Purpose

Close the evidence-binding gap between the multi-layer jurisdiction resolver in #132 and the existing pinned `axiom.education` v1 learner-event contract without changing that contract or its digest.

The existing v1 event has one optional `active_pack_manifest_sha256`. The jurisdiction resolver can return multiple simultaneous broad-to-specific standards layers. This PR makes the single v1 pack an explicit **event projection**, while preserving the complete ordered standards context in a sibling digest-bound evidence object.

